From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(musa): extend DSV4 score DeepGEMM to decode batches

The existing M<=16 guard only covered the single-request DSpark graph
shapes.  DSpark-4 FULL_DECODE_ONLY captures use M=20, 40, and 80 for
concurrency 4, 8, and 16.  MP56 measurements keep the BF16-to-FP32
DeepGEMM score projection faster than the fallback through M=80, so retain
the fast path for the production decode ladder while leaving long-prefill
shapes outside the guard.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py
index f87dc0b5b9..897fcdc7b2 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/attention.py
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ def _fill_short_context_topk_indices(
 
 
 # MUSA: the DeepSeek-V4 attention helpers below branch on the active platform.
-_MUSA_DEEPSEEK_V4_SCORE_FP32_DEEPGEMM_MAX_TOKENS = 16
+_MUSA_DEEPSEEK_V4_SCORE_FP32_DEEPGEMM_MAX_TOKENS = 80
 
 
 def _musa_deepseek_v4_serialize_long_prefill(num_tokens: int) -> bool:
